[00:00:00] Speaker_A: What does studying mean? And how do people usually approach this process?
[00:00:05] Speaker_A: And how do people perceive studying?
[00:00:07] Speaker_A: Studying means getting knowledge about something by reading, examining it in detail or researching.
[00:00:15] Speaker_A: We usually perceive studying to be hard and boring,
[00:00:18] Speaker_A: and something that you can usually complete and leave behind, like a course,
[00:00:23] Speaker_A: or when you study in school, you can't wait to finish it and forget about it.
[00:00:26] Speaker_A: When people think that they need to study English,
[00:00:29] Speaker_A: they usually think that they need to take a course or work with a teacher one-on-one for some time,
[00:00:35] Speaker_A: and that'll be enough. When they finish it, they will know English, and they won't need to go back to learning again.
[00:00:42] Speaker_A: Boy, are they wrong? Well, to be fair, to each his own.
[00:00:46] Speaker_A: If your goal is just to pass a test like IELTS, then yeah, you pass a test and you forget about it.
[00:00:52] Speaker_A: That's why it's important to determine your goal.
[00:00:55] Speaker_A: Do you need English to pass an exam or test?
[00:00:58] Speaker_A: Do you learn it for fun? Are you actually serious about it and you want to truly become fluent in English?
[00:01:04] Speaker_A: Do you need it for work or do you have an intention to move to an English-speaking country?
[00:01:08] Speaker_A: A lot of people do need to just pass the IELTS exam.
[00:01:12] Speaker_A: So they study for that, they get their band, and they just relax and stop,
[00:01:18] Speaker_A: because that was their goal. You can reach a certain level in English and maybe even a very good level,
[00:01:24] Speaker_A: but then what? If you just quit practicing and using English, your skills will worsen.
[00:01:30] Speaker_A: Of course, you can take breaks from learning.
[00:01:32] Speaker_A: If you go a month without saying a word in English and not listening to anything in English,
[00:01:37] Speaker_A: you'll be fine. But if this period expands to a year,
[00:01:42] Speaker_A: you most likely are going to have to work on some skills once again.
[00:01:46] Speaker_A: Especially speaking, and you might forget some vocabulary.
[00:01:50] Speaker_A: That's why I prefer living English.
[00:01:53] Speaker_A: What do I mean by living English?
[00:01:56] Speaker_A: You need to surround yourself by the English language so that you have no choice but to use it.
[00:02:02] Speaker_A: You need to incorporate it into your life so much so that it doesn't feel like learning anymore,
[00:02:07] Speaker_A: but is just a part of your everyday life, part of your routine.
[00:02:12] Speaker_A: This way, you will not forget English, you will not lose your skills.
